# v1.5.7 090f — sdist additions for the custom build backend.
#
# pyproject.toml declares `build-backend = "_qpb_build_backend"`
# with `backend-path = ["."]` (090c). When `python -m build`
# (the standard publish path) runs the sdist→wheel sequence, it
# unpacks the sdist and tries to import `_qpb_build_backend`
# from the unpacked tree. Without this MANIFEST.in entry, the
# backend module is NOT included in the sdist and the wheel
# build fails with:
#
#   pyproject_hooks._impl.BackendUnavailable: Cannot find module
#   '_qpb_build_backend' in ['…/quality_playbook-1.5.7']
#
# Shipping the backend in the sdist closes that gap. The backend
# itself (post-090f T-A2) is context-aware: when run from a
# source tree it stages + stamps; when run from an unpacked
# sdist (where the bundle is already complete + version is
# already stamped) it skips and delegates straight to setuptools.
#
# Note we do NOT ship the root `bin/` or any other dev machinery
# — the sdist stays the lean runtime+bundle artifact, with only
# the one backend module added.
include _qpb_build_backend.py
